{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29899 - PROTEIN:5840",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between the compound [(1S,3S,4S,6S,9R,10S,11S,13S,14S,16S)-3-acetyloxy-16-hydroxy-13-(hydroxymethyl)-5,5,9-trimethyl-12-oxapentacyclo[11.2.1.111,14.01,10.04,9]heptadecan-6-yl] acetate and the cell line H9, through a series of intermediate targets. The compound is identified as a target of Leosibirone B and another compound, (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, which in turn targets H9. Additionally, the compound is linked to Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is also a target of 5-Oxobrucine, which again targets H9. This suggests that the compound may act through multiple pathways, possibly by modulating microtubule dynamics or by directly interacting with sialyltransferase activity, which is involved in cell surface glycosylation. The evidence is consistent with the compound being a potential modulator of H9 cell behavior, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
